    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Differentiate clearly between Active Immunity (body produces its own antibodies) and Passive Immunity (ready-made antibodies introduced into the body).",
        "Memorize major nutritional deficiency diseases: Vitamin A (Night Blindness), Vitamin C (Scurvy), Vitamin D (Rickets), Iron (Anaemia), and Iodine (Goitre).",
        "Edward Jenner is frequently asked as the pioneer who developed the first successful smallpox vaccine in 1796.",
        "Disease vectors are crucial exam topics: Female Anopheles mosquito causes Malaria, while Aedes aegypti mosquito transmits Dengue and Chikungunya."
      ],
      "id": "evai84i"
